{
  "@context": {
    "@vocab": "https://activeflights.com/specs/v1/ssim#",
    "rdf": "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#",
    "rdfs": "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#",
    "xsd": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#",
    "iata": "https://www.iata.org/",
    "ssim": "https://activeflights.com/specs/v1/ssim#",
    "field": "https://activeflights.com/specs/v1/field#",
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "SSIMSpecification",
  "@id": "ssim.ch7",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "name": "IATA SSIM Chapter 7 - Schedule Data Interchange",
  "iataChapter": "7",
  "iataVersion": "2025.35",
  "status": "active",

  "description": "Complete IATA Standard Schedules Information Manual (SSIM) Chapter 7 specification for flight schedule data interchange. Defines 5 fixed-width record types (RT1-RT5) with 200-byte format for exchanging airline schedule data between carriers, GDSs, and aviation systems.",

  "aiNotes": "SSIM Chapter 7 - Master specification for flight schedule interchange.\n\nKEY CONCEPTS:\n\n1. **Fixed-Width Format**: All records are exactly 200 bytes\n   - Enables fast sequential parsing\n   - No delimiters needed (position-based)\n   - Legacy mainframe compatibility\n\n2. **5 Record Types**:\n   - RT1 (Header): File signature, appears once\n   - RT2 (Carrier): Opens carrier schedule block\n   - RT3 (Flight Leg): Individual flight details\n   - RT4 (Segment Data): Additional flight data (DEI-based)\n   - RT5 (Trailer): Closes carrier block, integrity check\n\n3. **Hierarchical Structure**:\n   ```\n   RT1 → [RT2 → [RT3 → [RT4]*]* → RT5]* → EOF\n   ```\n   - One RT1 per file\n   - Multiple carriers (RT2/RT5 pairs)\n   - Multiple flights per carrier\n   - Multiple segments per flight\n\n4. **Zero-Based Indexing**:\n   - Byte positions are 0-indexed (0-199)\n   - Aligns with programming language arrays\n   - IATA docs use 1-based (1-200) - convert when implementing\n\n5. **Encoding Support**:\n   - ASCII (most common)\n   - EBCDIC (legacy mainframe)\n   - All specs support both encodings\n\n6. **Block Structure**:\n   - 1000-byte blocks (5 records × 200 bytes)\n   - Zero-padding after final record in block\n   - Legacy tape/mainframe requirement\n\n7. **Serial Number Tracking**:\n   - Every record has sequential serial number\n   - RT1 always = 000001\n   - Increment by 1 for each record\n   - Detects missing/duplicate records\n   - Overflow: 999999 → 000002 (skip 000001)\n\n8. **Data Element Identifiers (DEI)**:\n   - RT4 uses DEI codes (001-999)\n   - DEI defines format of 155-byte segment_data payload\n   - 60+ DEI types defined in Chapter 2\n   - Examples: DEI 106 (booking classes), DEI 001 (joint operation)\n\nPARSING ARCHITECTURE:\n\nParser should implement:\n\n1. **Record-level parsing**:\n   - Read 200-byte blocks\n   - Detect record type (byte 0)\n   - Dispatch to type-specific parser\n   - Validate serial number sequence\n\n2. **Field-level parsing**:\n   - Extract fields by position (zero-indexed)\n   - Apply type conversion (string → int, date, etc.)\n   - Trim padding (blanks, zeros)\n   - Validate against field specs\n\n3. **Semantic validation**:\n   - Cross-record relationships (RT4 → RT3, RT5 → RT2)\n   - File structure hierarchy\n   - Serial number integrity\n   - Block padding\n\n4. **Error handling**:\n   - Field validation errors (collect all, don't fail fast)\n   - Record structure errors (reject record)\n   - File structure errors (reject file)\n   - Overflow handling (log warnings)\n\n5. **Extensions**:\n   - Computed fields (file_integrity, record_type_summary)\n   - Parsed segment data (DEI-based)\n   - Processing metadata (timestamps, checksums)\n\nOPTIMIZATION PATTERNS:\n\n1. **String interning**: Reuse strings (airline codes, airport codes)\n2. **Spec singletons**: Share field metadata across records\n3. **Concurrent parsing**: Process chunks in parallel\n4. **Direct byte access**: Avoid intermediate string allocations\n5. **Lazy extensions**: Compute only when accessed\n\nUSE CASES:\n\n1. **Schedule distribution**: Airlines publish schedules\n2. **GDS ingestion**: Travel systems import schedules\n3. **Code-share coordination**: Partners exchange data\n4. **Network planning**: Route/capacity analysis\n5. **Regulatory reporting**: Submit schedules to authorities",

  "sharedVocabulary": {
    "@ref": "./shared.vocabulary.jsonld",
    "description": "Common field definitions, types, and patterns used across all record types"
  },

  "recordTypes": [
    {
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_1",
      "@ref": "./header.spec.jsonld",
      "recordType": 1,
      "name": "Header Record (RT1)",
      "description": "File header signature. Always first record in file (serial 000001). Contains file metadata and title.",
      "cardinality": "exactly-one",
      "position": "file-start",
      "keyFields": ["record_type", "title_of_contents", "data_set_serial_number"],
      "aiNotes": "RT1 marks file start. Every SSIM file begins with RT1 at serial 000001. Contains 'AIRLINE STANDARD SCHEDULE DATA SET' signature."
    },
    {
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_2",
      "@ref": "./carrier.spec.jsonld",
      "recordType": 2,
      "name": "Carrier Record (RT2)",
      "description": "Opens carrier schedule block. Defines airline, period of validity, time mode. Each RT2 is closed by corresponding RT5.",
      "cardinality": "one-or-more",
      "position": "after-rt1-or-rt5",
      "keyFields": ["record_type", "airline_designator", "period_of_validity_from", "period_of_validity_to"],
      "aiNotes": "RT2 opens carrier block. Can have multiple carriers per file (RT2/RT5 pairs). Contains schedule validity dates and time mode."
    },
    {
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3",
      "@ref": "./flight.spec.jsonld",
      "recordType": 3,
      "name": "Flight Leg Record (RT3)",
      "description": "Individual flight leg data. Contains flight identity, routing, timing, aircraft, service type. Most complex record (50+ fields).",
      "cardinality": "zero-or-more-per-carrier",
      "position": "within-rt2-block",
      "keyFields": ["record_type", "airline_designator", "flight_number", "departure_station", "arrival_station"],
      "linkFields": {
        "to": "RT2",
        "via": ["airline_designator"]
      },
      "aiNotes": "RT3 defines flight leg. Contains routing (DEP→ARR), times, aircraft type, days of operation. Can have multiple RT4 segment records."
    },
    {
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_4",
      "@ref": "./segment.spec.jsonld",
      "recordType": 4,
      "name": "Segment Data Record (RT4)",
      "description": "Additional flight data. DEI-based format with 155-byte segment_data payload. Multiple RT4s can link to one RT3 (different DEIs).",
      "cardinality": "zero-or-more-per-flight",
      "position": "after-rt3",
      "keyFields": ["record_type", "airline_designator", "flight_number", "data_element_identifier"],
      "linkFields": {
        "to": "RT3",
        "via": ["airline_designator", "flight_number", "itinerary_variation_identifier", "leg_sequence_number", "service_type"]
      },
      "aiNotes": "RT4 provides supplemental flight data. Links to RT3 via composite key. DEI (bytes 30-32) defines segment_data format. Common DEIs: 106 (booking), 001 (joint operation)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_5",
      "@ref": "./trailer.spec.jsonld",
      "recordType": 5,
      "name": "Trailer Record (RT5)",
      "description": "Closes carrier block. Contains serial number check reference and continuation/end code. Enables file integrity validation.",
      "cardinality": "exactly-one-per-carrier",
      "position": "end-of-rt2-block",
      "keyFields": ["record_type", "airline_designator", "serial_number_check_reference", "continuation_end_code"],
      "linkFields": {
        "to": "RT2",
        "via": ["airline_designator"]
      },
      "aiNotes": "RT5 closes carrier block opened by RT2. continuation_end_code: 'C'=more carriers follow, 'E'=end of file. serial_number_check_reference enables integrity checking."
    }
  ],

  "fileStructure": {
    "@id": "ssim.ch7.file_structure",
    "name": "SSIM File Structure",
    "description": "Defines the hierarchical organization and constraints of SSIM files.",

    "recordLength": 200,
    "recordLengthDescription": "All records are exactly 200 bytes (fixed-width format)",

    "blockSize": 1000,
    "blockSizeDescription": "Records are organized in 1000-byte blocks (5 records per block)",

    "recordsPerBlock": 5,

    "blockPadding": {
      "type": "zero",
      "description": "After final record in block, pad remaining bytes with zeros (0x30 ASCII, 0xF0 EBCDIC) to reach 1000-byte boundary",
      "ascii_char": "0",
      "ebcdic_hex": "0xF0"
    },

    "encoding": ["ASCII", "EBCDIC"],
    "encodingDescription": "Files can use either ASCII or EBCDIC character encoding. ASCII is most common.",

    "indexing": {
      "type": "zero-based",
      "description": "Byte positions are zero-indexed (0-199 for 200-byte records). This aligns with programming language array indexing.",
      "note": "IATA SSIM documentation uses 1-based indexing (1-200). Implementations should use 0-based for direct byte array access."
    },

    "hierarchicalStructure": {
      "description": "SSIM files follow strict hierarchical structure with enforced ordering and relationships",
      "pattern": "RT1 → [RT2 → [RT3 → [RT4]*]* → RT5]* → EOF",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0,
          "recordType": "RT1",
          "name": "File",
          "cardinality": "1",
          "description": "Exactly one header per file"
        },
        {
          "level": 1,
          "recordType": "RT2/RT5",
          "name": "Carrier Block",
          "cardinality": "1..N",
          "description": "One or more carrier blocks (RT2 opens, RT5 closes)"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "recordType": "RT3",
          "name": "Flight Leg",
          "cardinality": "0..N",
          "description": "Zero or more flights per carrier"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "recordType": "RT4",
          "name": "Segment Data",
          "cardinality": "0..N",
          "description": "Zero or more segments per flight"
        }
      ]
    },

    "sequencing": {
      "description": "Records must appear in specific order with sequential serial numbers",
      "rules": [
        "RT1 always first (serial 000001)",
        "RT2 opens carrier block",
        "RT3 records follow RT2 (within same carrier)",
        "RT4 records follow RT3 (link to specific flight)",
        "RT5 closes carrier block",
        "continuation_end_code determines if more carriers follow",
        "Serial numbers increment by 1 for each record (no gaps)",
        "Overflow at 999999 wraps to 000002 (skip 000001)"
      ]
    }
  },

  "relationships": {
    "@id": "ssim.ch7.relationships",
    "name": "Cross-Record Relationships",
    "description": "Defines how record types link together to form a coherent schedule dataset.",

    "graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Relationship",
        "id": "rt1_precedes_rt2",
        "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_1",
        "target": "ssim.ch7.record_type_2",
        "relationType": "precedes",
        "cardinality": "1:N",
        "description": "RT1 is followed by one or more RT2 carrier blocks",
        "validation": "First RT2 must have serial_number = 000002 (immediately after RT1)"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Relationship",
        "id": "rt2_contains_rt3",
        "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_2",
        "target": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3",
        "relationType": "contains",
        "cardinality": "1:N",
        "description": "RT2 carrier block contains zero or more RT3 flight legs",
        "linkFields": ["airline_designator"],
        "validation": "RT3.airline_designator must match RT2.airline_designator"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Relationship",
        "id": "rt3_has_rt4",
        "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3",
        "target": "ssim.ch7.record_type_4",
        "relationType": "hasSegments",
        "cardinality": "1:N",
        "description": "RT3 flight may have zero or more RT4 segment data records",
        "linkFields": ["airline_designator", "flight_number", "itinerary_variation_identifier", "leg_sequence_number", "service_type"],
        "validation": "RT4 must link to existing RT3 via composite key (airline + flight + itinerary + leg + service)"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Relationship",
        "id": "rt2_closed_by_rt5",
        "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_2",
        "target": "ssim.ch7.record_type_5",
        "relationType": "closedBy",
        "cardinality": "1:1",
        "description": "Each RT2 carrier block is closed by exactly one RT5 trailer",
        "linkFields": ["airline_designator"],
        "validation": "RT5.airline_designator should match RT2.airline_designator (warning if mismatch)"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Relationship",
        "id": "rt5_precedes_rt2",
        "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_5",
        "target": "ssim.ch7.record_type_2",
        "relationType": "precedes",
        "cardinality": "0:1",
        "description": "RT5 with continuation_end_code='C' is followed by another RT2. RT5 with 'E' is end-of-file.",
        "conditional": "continuation_end_code === 'C'",
        "validation": "If continuation_end_code='C', next record must be RT2. If 'E', expect EOF or block padding."
      }
    ]
  },

  "extensions": {
    "@id": "ssim.ch7.extensions",
    "name": "File-Level Extensions",
    "description": "Computed fields and metadata that apply to entire SSIM file after parsing.",

    "fields": [
      {
        "@type": "Extension",
        "@id": "ssim.ch7#ext_file_summary",
        "name": "file_summary",
        "description": "High-level summary of file contents. Computed after complete file parse.",
        "type": "object",
        "loadingStrategy": "computed",
        "properties": {
          "total_records": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Total number of records in file (should match RT5 serial_number)"
          },
          "total_bytes": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Total file size in bytes (total_records × 200)"
          },
          "record_counts": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "headers": {"type": "integer", "description": "Count of RT1 records (should be 1)"},
              "carriers": {"type": "integer", "description": "Count of RT2 records"},
              "flights": {"type": "integer", "description": "Count of RT3 records"},
              "segments": {"type": "integer", "description": "Count of RT4 records"},
              "trailers": {"type": "integer", "description": "Count of RT5 records (should equal carriers)"}
            }
          },
          "carriers": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "airline_designator": {"type": "string"},
                "flight_count": {"type": "integer"},
                "segment_count": {"type": "integer"},
                "period_from": {"type": "string", "format": "date"},
                "period_to": {"type": "string", "format": "date"}
              }
            },
            "description": "Summary of each carrier in file"
          },
          "encoding": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": ["ASCII", "EBCDIC"],
            "description": "Detected character encoding"
          },
          "is_valid": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "True if file passed all structural and semantic validations"
          }
        },
        "exampleUsage": "{\n  \"total_records\": 5432,\n  \"total_bytes\": 1086400,\n  \"record_counts\": {\n    \"headers\": 1,\n    \"carriers\": 3,\n    \"flights\": 3200,\n    \"segments\": 2225,\n    \"trailers\": 3\n  },\n  \"carriers\": [\n    {\n      \"airline_designator\": \"QF\",\n      \"flight_count\": 1500,\n      \"segment_count\": 1200,\n      \"period_from\": \"2025-01-01\",\n      \"period_to\": \"2025-12-31\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"airline_designator\": \"VA\",\n      \"flight_count\": 1000,\n      \"segment_count\": 800,\n      \"period_from\": \"2025-01-01\",\n      \"period_to\": \"2025-12-31\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"airline_designator\": \"JQ\",\n      \"flight_count\": 700,\n      \"segment_count\": 225,\n      \"period_from\": \"2025-01-01\",\n      \"period_to\": \"2025-06-30\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"encoding\": \"ASCII\",\n  \"is_valid\": true\n}",
        "aiNotes": "FILE SUMMARY: Top-level metrics for entire file.\n\nUsage:\n- Data quality dashboards\n- File completeness checks\n- Carrier statistics\n- Ingestion metrics\n\nComputation:\n```typescript\nfunction computeFileSummary(records: Record[]): FileSummary {\n  const counts = countRecordTypes(records);\n  const carriers = groupByCarrier(records.filter(r => r.record_type === '2'));\n  \n  return {\n    total_records: records.length,\n    total_bytes: records.length * 200,\n    record_counts: counts,\n    carriers: carriers.map(computeCarrierSummary),\n    encoding: detectEncoding(records),\n    is_valid: validateFile(records).valid\n  };\n}\n```"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Extension",
        "@id": "ssim.ch7#ext_integrity_report",
        "name": "integrity_report",
        "description": "Comprehensive integrity validation report. Identifies missing records, structural errors, and data quality issues.",
        "type": "object",
        "loadingStrategy": "computed",
        "properties": {
          "has_header": {"type": "boolean", "description": "True if RT1 exists with serial 000001"},
          "header_valid": {"type": "boolean", "description": "True if RT1 has correct signature"},
          "carrier_blocks_valid": {"type": "boolean", "description": "True if all RT2/RT5 pairs are matched"},
          "serial_sequence_valid": {"type": "boolean", "description": "True if no gaps in serial numbers"},
          "structure_valid": {"type": "boolean", "description": "True if hierarchical structure is correct"},
          "missing_records": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer"}, "description": "List of missing serial numbers"},
          "orphaned_rt3": {"type": "array", "description": "RT3 records without matching RT2"},
          "orphaned_rt4": {"type": "array", "description": "RT4 records without matching RT3"},
          "unmatched_rt2_rt5": {"type": "array", "description": "RT2 records without closing RT5 or vice versa"},
          "block_padding_issues": {"type": "array", "description": "Blocks with incorrect padding"},
          "overflow_detected": {"type": "boolean", "description": "True if serial number overflow occurred (999999 → 000002)"},
          "error_count": {"type": "integer", "description": "Total number of errors detected"},
          "warning_count": {"type": "integer", "description": "Total number of warnings"},
          "is_complete": {"type": "boolean", "description": "True if file is structurally sound and complete"}
        },
        "aiNotes": "INTEGRITY REPORT: Comprehensive validation results.\n\nPurpose:\n- Pre-ingestion validation\n- Data quality metrics\n- Error reporting and alerting\n- File acceptance/rejection decisions\n\nUsage:\n```typescript\nconst report = computeIntegrityReport(records);\n\nif (!report.is_complete) {\n  console.error('File integrity check failed');\n  console.error(`Errors: ${report.error_count}`);\n  console.error(`Warnings: ${report.warning_count}`);\n  \n  if (report.missing_records.length > 0) {\n    console.error(`Missing records: ${report.missing_records}`);\n  }\n  \n  // Reject file or request resend\n  return rejectFile(report);\n}\n\n// File is valid, proceed with ingestion\nreturn ingestFile(records);\n```"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Extension",
        "@id": "ssim.ch7#ext_parsing_metadata",
        "name": "parsing_metadata",
        "description": "Metadata about the parsing operation itself. Useful for debugging, auditing, and performance monitoring.",
        "type": "object",
        "loadingStrategy": "computed",
        "properties": {
          "parser_version": {"type": "string", "description": "Version of parser used"},
          "parsed_at": {"type": "string", "format": "iso8601", "description": "Timestamp when file was parsed"},
          "parse_duration_ms": {"type": "integer", "description": "Time taken to parse file (milliseconds)"},
          "source_file": {"type": "string", "description": "Original filename"},
          "source_checksum": {"type": "string", "description": "SHA256 hash of source file"},
          "source_size_bytes": {"type": "integer", "description": "Source file size in bytes"},
          "detected_encoding": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ASCII", "EBCDIC"]},
          "records_per_second": {"type": "number", "description": "Parsing throughput"},
          "validation_duration_ms": {"type": "integer", "description": "Time taken for validation"}
        },
        "aiNotes": "PARSING METADATA: Audit trail for file processing.\n\nUsage:\n- Performance monitoring\n- Audit logs\n- Troubleshooting\n- Parser version tracking\n\nExample:\n```typescript\nconst metadata = {\n  parser_version: '1.0.0',\n  parsed_at: '2025-11-24T10:30:00Z',\n  parse_duration_ms: 450,\n  source_file: 'qantas_schedule_2025.ssim',\n  source_checksum: 'sha256:abc123...',\n  source_size_bytes: 1086400,\n  detected_encoding: 'ASCII',\n  records_per_second: 12071.1,\n  validation_duration_ms: 120\n};\n```"
      }
    ]
  },

  "semanticRules": {
    "@ref": "./shared.vocabulary.jsonld#sharedSemanticRules",
    "description": "Shared validation rules that apply across record types. See shared.vocabulary.jsonld for detailed definitions.",
    "summary": [
      "sr.fixed_length_200: All records must be exactly 200 bytes",
      "sr.record_serial_overflow: Serial numbers wrap from 999999 to 000002",
      "sr.block_padding: Pad to 1000-byte blocks with zeros after RT5",
      "sr.file_structure: Enforce hierarchical RT1 → RT2 → RT3 → RT4 → RT5 structure"
    ]
  },

  "implementationGuidance": {
    "@id": "ssim.ch7.implementation_guidance",
    "name": "Parser Implementation Guidance",
    "description": "Recommendations for building efficient, correct SSIM parsers.",

    "architecture": {
      "description": "Recommended parser architecture patterns",
      "layers": [
        {
          "name": "Byte Reader",
          "description": "Read 200-byte chunks from file (binary mode)",
          "responsibilities": ["File I/O", "Block boundary detection", "Padding handling"]
        },
        {
          "name": "Record Parser",
          "description": "Detect record type and dispatch to type-specific parser",
          "responsibilities": ["Type detection (byte 0)", "Dispatch to RT1-RT5 parsers", "Serial number tracking"]
        },
        {
          "name": "Field Extractor",
          "description": "Extract fields by position using spec metadata",
          "responsibilities": ["Position-based extraction", "Type conversion", "Padding trimming", "Field validation"]
        },
        {
          "name": "Semantic Validator",
          "description": "Validate cross-record relationships and file structure",
          "responsibilities": ["Hierarchy validation", "Link validation (RT4→RT3, RT5→RT2)", "Integrity checks"]
        },
        {
          "name": "Extension Computator",
          "description": "Compute derived fields and metadata",
          "responsibilities": ["file_summary", "integrity_report", "parsing_metadata"]
        }
      ]
    },

    "performanceOptimizations": [
      {
        "name": "String Interning",
        "description": "Reuse string instances for repeated values (airline codes, airport codes)",
        "impact": "60-70% memory reduction for typical files",
        "example": "'LAX' appears 1000 times → 1 allocation instead of 1000"
      },
      {
        "name": "Spec Singletons",
        "description": "Share field metadata across all records (don't embed in each record)",
        "impact": "1000× memory savings for large files",
        "example": "1 HeaderSpec shared by 100K records"
      },
      {
        "name": "Concurrent Parsing",
        "description": "Process file chunks in parallel (split on 1000-byte block boundaries)",
        "impact": "Linear scaling with CPU cores",
        "example": "8 cores = ~8× throughput"
      },
      {
        "name": "Direct Byte Access",
        "description": "Extract fields directly from byte arrays without intermediate string allocations",
        "impact": "50% fewer allocations, 2× faster parsing",
        "example": "Read integer fields as bytes, parse in-place"
      },
      {
        "name": "Lazy Extensions",
        "description": "Compute extension fields only when accessed (not during parse)",
        "impact": "Skip expensive computations if not needed",
        "example": "Don't compute integrity_report if caller only needs record_counts"
      }
    ],

    "errorHandling": [
      {
        "category": "Fatal Errors",
        "description": "Errors that prevent parsing (reject file immediately)",
        "examples": ["Record length ≠ 200 bytes", "Invalid record type", "RT1 missing", "File truncated"]
      },
      {
        "category": "Structural Errors",
        "description": "Errors in file structure (reject file, request resend)",
        "examples": ["RT2 without RT5", "RT4 without matching RT3", "Serial number gaps", "Invalid hierarchy"]
      },
      {
        "category": "Field Errors",
        "description": "Errors in individual fields (collect, report, may accept file)",
        "examples": ["Invalid date format", "Out-of-range value", "Pattern mismatch", "Missing mandatory field"]
      },
      {
        "category": "Warnings",
        "description": "Issues that don't prevent parsing (log, continue)",
        "examples": ["Serial overflow", "Block padding incorrect", "Unknown DEI code", "Airline mismatch in RT5"]
      }
    ],

    "testingRecommendations": [
      {
        "category": "Unit Tests",
        "description": "Test individual record type parsers with synthetic data",
        "coverage": ["Field extraction", "Type conversion", "Validation", "Edge cases"]
      },
      {
        "category": "Integration Tests",
        "description": "Test full file parsing with real SSIM files",
        "coverage": ["Multi-carrier files", "Large files (100K+ records)", "Overflow scenarios", "Error conditions"]
      },
      {
        "category": "Property-Based Tests",
        "description": "Generate random valid SSIM data, parse, validate round-trip",
        "coverage": ["Marshal → Unmarshal → Marshal", "All field combinations", "Boundary values"]
      },
      {
        "category": "Performance Tests",
        "description": "Benchmark parsing speed, memory usage, concurrency",
